<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Meštrović</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a>–<a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Meštrović was a Croatian sculptor and architect, one of the leading sculptors of the twentieth century. A supporter of South Slav unity and a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslav-committee">Yugoslav Committee</a>, he created monumental works including the Monument to the Unknown Hero on Mount Avala, the Victor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> and the statue of Gregory of Nin in Split. He emigrated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-mestrovic.jpg" alt="Ivan Meštrović" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Grantham Bain Collection (Library of Congress) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ivan_Me%C5%A1trovic.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
